*                        THE DG IS USED TO CREATE THE PARAMETER LISTS * 16900002
*                        FOR THE EXITS. THE BYTE AFTER THE EXIT NAME  * 16950002
*                        IN FIELD IS TESTED FOR '01'. IF IT IS X'01', * 17000002
*                        THE 3 LETTER EXIT NAME IS MOVED INTO DDNAMES * 17050002
*                        (THE PARAMETER LIST TO DG), AND THE DG IS    * 17100002
*                        ATTACHED. TESTEXIT WAITS UNTIL THE DG POSTS  * 17150002
*                        ITS ECB THAT IT IS FINISHED. IF A NON-ZERO   * 17200002
*                        CODE IS RETURNED, AN ERROR MESSAGE IS        * 17250002
*                        WRITTEN AND THE EXIT IS NOT CALLED.          * 17300002
*                        OTHERWISE, THE OUTPUT DATA SET FROM THE DG   * 17350002
*                        IS OPENED FOR INPUT IN ORDER TO READ THE     * 17400002
*                        PARAMETER LISTS INTO TESTEXIT WORK AREA. IF  * 17450002
*                        THE DATA SET DOES NOT OPEN CORRECTLY, AN     * 17500002
*                        ERROR MESSAGE IS WRITTEN AND THE EXIT IS NOT * 17550002
*                        CALLED. THE ADDRESS OF THE OPEN DCB IS PUT   * 17600002
*                        INTO OPENADDR. THE DCB IS TESTED FOR FIXED OR* 17650002
*                        VARIABLE RECORD FORMAT. IF THE RECFM IS      * 17700002
*                        FIXED, SWITCH IS SET TO X'01' AND THE LOGICAL* 17750002
*                        RECORD LENGTH IS SAVED IN FLRECL. A BLANK    * 17800002
*                        LINE AND THE EXIT NAME ARE WRITTEN TO        * 17850002
*                        SYSPRINT. THIS SECTION THEN BAL'S TO THE     * 17900002
*                        SECTION TO CALL THE EXIT ROUTINE. UPON       * 17950002
*                        RETURN, THE DCB IS CLOSED AND THE NEXT EXIT  * 18000002
*                        NAME IS TESTED. AFTER ALL EXITS HAVE BEEN    * 18050002
*                        TESTED FOR THE CALL INDICATOR, THIS SECTION  * 18100002
*                        BRANCHES TO ENDUP TO RETURN TO THE SYSTEM.   * 18150002
* ENTRIES - INITIALLY FROM PARMPROS - PARAMETER PROCESSING            * 18200002
* EXITS  - FINALLY TO ENDUP TO RETURN TO THE SYSTEM                   * 18250002
* SUBROUTINES - 1. DATA GENERATOR-IEBDG  TO GENERATE PARAMETER LIST   * 18300002
*                  FOR EACH EXIT TO BE CALLED                         * 18350002
*               2. WAIT ROUTINES TO WAIT FOR DG TO COMPLETE           * 18400002
*               3. DETACH TO DETACH DG AFTER EACH USE                 * 18450002
*               4. OPEN TO OPEN OUTPUT DATA SETS FROM DG FOR INPUT TO * 18500002
*                  TESTEXIT.                                          * 18550002
*               5. WRITEMSG TO WRITE BLANK LINE                       * 18600002
*               6. MAKEMSG TO WRITE EXIT 3 LETTER NAME                * 18650002
*               7. CALL EXIT SECTIONS TO CALL THE USER EXIT ROUTINES. * 18700002
*               8. CLOSE TO CLOSE THE OUTPUT DATA SET FROM THE DG.    * 18750002
*               9. DGERROR TO WRITE ERROR MESSAGE FOR DG ERROR.       * 18800002
*               10. OPENERROR TO WRITE ERROR MESSAGE IF DATA SET DOES * 18850002
*                   NOT OPEN CORRECTLY.                               * 18900002
* INPUT - 1. NUMBERS CONTAINS THE NUMBER OF CALLS TO EACH EXIT        * 18950002
*         2. FIELD CONTAINS A X'01' IN THE BYTE FOLLOWING THE EXIT    * 19000002
*            CALL LETTERS IF THE EXIT IS TO BE CALLED.                * 19050002
* TABLES - 1. FIELD - SEE PREVIOUS DESCRIPTION                        * 19100002
*          2. NUMBERS - SEE PREVIOUS DESCRIPTION                      * 19150002
*          3. DDNAMES - THE PARAMETER LIST FOR DG.  IT MUST BE ON A   * 19200002
*             HALF-WORD BOUNDARY. THE FIRST 2 BYTES CONTAIN THE LENGTH* 19250002
*             OF THE LIST EXCLUDING THE FIRST 2 BYTES. THE DDNAME FOR * 19300002
*             SYSIN IS IN DDNAMES+34 AND FOR SYSPRINT IN DDNAMES+42.  * 19350002
*             THE DOUBLE WORDS FOLLOWING THE 2 BYTE LENGTH MUST BE ON * 19400002
*             DOUBLE-WORD BOUNDARIES. AS EACH EXIT IS SETUP, THE 3    * 19450002
*             CALL LETTERS ARE PLACED AFTER 'IN' SO THE DG WILL KNOW  * 19500002
*             WHICH DATA SET TO USE AS SYSIN.                         * 19550002
